<article class="env-lemma" id="6BB2E9">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/6BB2E9">Lemma <span data-tag="6BB2E9">6.1.4.5</span>.</a> Let $\calX $ be a presentable $\infty $-category and let $f: U_{\bullet }^{+} \rightarrow V_{\bullet }^{+}$ be a map of simplicial resolutions which exhibits $V_{\bullet }^{+}$ as the groupoid resolution generated by $U_{\bullet }^{+}$. Let $W_{\bullet }^{+}$ be an augmented simplicial object of $\calX $ such that the underlying simplicial object $W_{\bullet } \in \calX _{\Delta }$ is a groupoid. Composition with $f$ induces a homotopy equivalence </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \bHom _{\calX _{\Delta _{+}}}( V_{\bullet }^{+}, W_{\bullet }^{+} ) \rightarrow \bHom _{\calX _{\Delta _{+}}}( U_{\bullet }^{+}, W_{\bullet }^{+} ). \]
</div>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $|W_{\bullet }|$ be a colimit of $W_{\bullet }$. Then we have a commutative diagram 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { \bHom _{\calX _{\Delta _{+}}}( V_{\bullet }^{+}, |W_{\bullet }| ) \ar [r] \ar [d] &amp;  \bHom _{\calX _{\Delta _{+}}}( U_{\bullet }^{+}, |W_{\bullet }| ) \ar [d] \\ \bHom _{\calX _{\Delta _{+}}}( V_{\bullet }^{+}, W_{\bullet }^{+} ) \ar [r] &amp;  \bHom _{\calX _{\Delta _{+}}}( U_{\bullet }^{+}, W_{\bullet }^{+} )}  \]
</div>
    <p>
       where the vertical maps are homotopy equivalences (since $U_{\bullet }^{+}$ and $V_{\bullet }^{+}$ are resolutions) and the upper horizontal map is a homotopy equivalence (since $|W_{\bullet }|$ is a groupoid resolution). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>